---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
    title="SF Ruby News - May 2026"
    description="May 2026 edition of SF Ruby News: GitHub adopts Herb across 500K lines of ERB. Matz ships AI-built Spinel compiler. Stripe reveals 50M-line Ruby monorepo. Chime first GAAP profit. Shopify, Block, Airbnb, Instacart, Omada break Q1 records. Rails World 2026 heads to Austin."
>
    <section class="relative bg-gradient-to-b from-gray-950 via-gray-900 to-gray-950 text-white overflow-hidden min-h-screen">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-ruby-950/30"></div>
        <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 relative z-10 pt-32 pb-16">

            <!-- Issue Navigation -->
            <div class="flex items-center justify-between mb-8 text-sm">
                <a href="/news/2026-04/" class="text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors flex items-center gap-1">
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7" /></svg>
                    April 2026
                </a>
                <a href="/news/2026-06/" class="text-white/50 hover:text-white transition-colors flex items-center gap-1">
                    June 2026
                    <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7" /></svg>
                </a>
            </div>

            <!-- Masthead -->
            <div class="text-center mb-12">
                <div class="flex items-center gap-4 justify-center mb-3">
                    <div class="flex-1 max-w-[120px] h-px bg-white/20"></div>
                    <a href="/#news" class="font-display text-2xl md:text-3xl tracking-wider uppercase text-white font-bold hover:text-ruby-400 transition-colors">SF Ruby News</a>
                    <div class="flex-1 max-w-[120px] h-px bg-white/20"></div>
                </div>
                <p class="text-sm text-white/50 tracking-widest uppercase">May 2026</p>
            </div>

            <!-- News Carousel -->
            <div class="relative" id="news-carousel">

                <!-- Page 1 -->
                <div class="news-page" data-page="0">
                    <!-- Headline Story: GitHub adopts Herb -->
                    <div class="mb-10">
                        <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-4">Ruby at Scale</span>
                        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">GitHub Adopts Herb Across 500K Lines of ERB</h2>
                        <div class="border-l-2 border-ruby-500/60 pl-6">
                            <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
                                <strong class="text-white">Joel Hawksley</strong>, staff engineer on the github.com Rails monolith, publishes the inside story: <strong class="text-white">Rails core wants Herb to replace Erubi</strong>, and GitHub — rendering ERB at the largest scale of any Rails app — was asked to validate the parser.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mt-4">
                                500,000 lines of ERB across 10,000 files. 2,768 files initially failed Herb parsing. Herb caught markup and Ruby errors <code class="text-white/80">erb_lint</code> had missed (~150 mismatched-tag cases alone). Marco Roth's <a href="https://github.com/marcoroth/herb/releases/tag/v0.10.0" class="underline hover:text-white/80">Herb v0.10</a> shipped the same week — diff engine, dev server, and the foundation for reactive ERB rendering.
                            </p>
                            <div class="mt-4">
                                <p class="text-xs text-white/50">May 6, 2026 · hawksley.org</p>
                            </div>
                            <a href="https://hawksley.org/2026/05/06/adopting-herb-at-github.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 mt-3 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Read the post
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Divider -->
                    <div class="h-px bg-white/10 mb-10"></div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 1 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-10">
                        <!-- AI + Ruby: Matz Spinel -->
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">AI + Ruby</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Matz Ships an AI-Built Ruby Compiler</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">Apr 24, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">At RubyKaigi 2026, Matz unveils <strong class="text-white/80">Spinel</strong> — a native Ruby AOT compiler 11.6× faster than MiniRuby on Ruby 4.1. Ruby → AST → C → native binary. A three-year-old idea, implemented in weeks with Claude Code. MIT, 1.5K stars in two weeks.</p>
                            <a href="https://www.theregister.com/devops/2026/05/06/ruby-inventor-matz-working-on-native-compiler-with-ai-help/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Stripe — merged CI + Sessions -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-violet-500/20 text-violet-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Release</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Stripe: 50M-Line Ruby CI + 288 at Sessions</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">Apr 9 · Apr 29–May 1, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">SF Ruby company (Sinatra + internal framework) bookends April with two big signals. Aditya Anchuri details Stripe's <strong class="text-white/80">50-million-line Ruby monolith</strong> and Selective Test Execution (~5% of tests per PR). Days later: <a href="https://stripe.com/newsroom/news/sessions-2026" class="underline hover:text-white/80">288 Sessions launches</a> — Agentic Commerce with Meta/Google, AI-agent wallet, 9,000 attendees at Moscone.</p>
                            <a href="https://stripe.dev/blog/selective-test-execution-at-stripe-fast-ci-for-a-50m-line-ruby-monorepo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 transition-colors">
                                Read the CI post
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Intercom Fin for Sales -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-violet-500/20 text-violet-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Release</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Intercom Launches Fin for Sales</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">Apr 24, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">Fin moves beyond support. New Fin for Sales qualifies leads, books meetings, starts trials; Fin Copilot adds a free tier (10 conversations/month per agent); Fin Insights ships CX Score. Fin growing 350% YoY across 8,000 companies — all on a 2M-line Rails monolith.</p>
                            <a href="https://siliconangle.com/2026/04/24/intercoms-customer-service-agent-takes-new-sales-role/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 2 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-6">
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-violet-500/20 text-violet-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Release</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">RubyLLM 1.15: Image Editing + Cost Tracking</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Carmine Paolino's RubyLLM (≈5M downloads) ships image editing via <code class="text-white/80">paint</code>, conversation cost tracking with cache-read/write buckets, and Action Text plain-text extraction so HTML doesn't leak into prompts. Now the de-facto Ruby LangChain.</p>
                                <a href="https://github.com/crmne/ruby_llm/releases/tag/1.15.0" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 transition-colors">
                                    View release
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Event</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">SF Ruby Meetup, May @ Checkr</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Thursday May 21, 5pm, One Montgomery St. Kurt Ude (Checkr) on engineering fraud at enterprise scale, Waldemar Quevedo (Synadia) on building agents in Ruby with DSPy, and Pranav Raj (Chatwoot CEO, YC W21). 116+ RSVPs.</p>
                                <a href="https://luma.com/eyizxwjt" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                    RSVP on Luma
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Event</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Rails World 2026: Austin, AI Track, 1,200 Seats</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Rails Foundation announces the biggest Rails World yet: Austin, Sep 23–24, 1,200-attendee capacity, dedicated AI / Agentic Systems and Trust &amp; Security tracks. CFP closes May 16. General admission ($699) on sale May 12, 10am CT.</p>
                                <a href="https://rubyonrails.org/2026/4/23/big-rails-world-2026-update-CFP" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read announcement
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 3 (Community + Ecosystem) -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-6">
                        <!-- Event: Blue Ridge Ruby 2026 -->
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Event</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Blue Ridge Ruby 2026 in Asheville</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Two-day, single-track conference (April 30 - May 1), 21 talks. Agent thread again: "LLM Telemetry as a First-Class Rails Concern," "Instillment of Successful Practices in an Agentic World," a lightning talk on "Teaching Claude Code to Upgrade Rails." Joël Quenneville, Rachael Wright-Munn, Katya Sarmiento, Ifat Ribon on the bill.</p>
                                <a href="https://blueridgeruby.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                    See the lineup
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Press: Gusto Joins Ruby Alliance -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Press</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Gusto Joins Ruby Alliance</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Ruby Central launches the Ruby Alliance — a coalition of companies investing in long-term Ruby ecosystem health, resilience, and sustainability. SF-based $9.5B Rails unicorn Gusto signs on as the inaugural member (May 11).</p>
                                <a href="https://rubycentral.org/news/gusto-joins-the-ruby-alliance/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read announcement
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Event: Blastoff Rails 2026 -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Event</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Blastoff Rails 2026: Save the Date</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">June 11-12 in Albuquerque, NM. 9 talks, keynotes from Irina Nazarova (Evil Martians) and Kieran Klaassen. Topics: "How to Become a Famous Ruby/Rails Agentic Developer," "Why We're Still Training Rails Developers in an Age of AI," "Fewer Tests, More Confidence."</p>
                                <a href="https://www.blastoffrails.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                    See speakers
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Page 2 -->
                <div class="news-page hidden" data-page="1">
                    <!-- Headline Story: Q1 earnings -->
                    <div class="mb-10">
                        <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-ruby-500/20 text-ruby-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-4">Earnings</span>
                        <h2 class="font-display text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">Public Rails Companies Print Records</h2>
                        <div class="border-l-2 border-ruby-500/60 pl-6">
                            <p class="text-lg md:text-xl text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
                                <strong class="text-white">Chime</strong> turned its first GAAP-profitable quarter as a public company. <strong class="text-white">Shopify</strong> crossed $100B GMV. <strong class="text-white">Block</strong> printed a record $2.91B in gross profit.
                            </p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mt-4">
                                Chime: $647M revenue (+25%), 10.2M members, $53M net income. <strong class="text-white/80">Instacart</strong> hit its first $1B revenue quarter. <strong class="text-white/80">Airbnb</strong> $2.7B (+18%). <strong class="text-white/80">Procore</strong> $359M (+16%). All running Rails.
                            </p>
                            <div class="mt-4">
                                <p class="text-xs text-white/50">Q1 2026 results · May 5–7, 2026</p>
                            </div>
                            <a href="https://investors.chime.com/news-releases/news-release-details/chime-reports-first-quarter-2026-financial-results" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 mt-3 text-xs text-ruby-400 hover:text-ruby-300 transition-colors">
                                Read Chime Q1 release
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M10 6H6a2 2 0 00-2 2v10a2 2 0 002 2h10a2 2 0 002-2v-4M14 4h6m0 0v6m0-6L10 14" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Divider -->
                    <div class="h-px bg-white/10 mb-10"></div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 1 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-10">
                        <!-- Release: AngelList USVC -->
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-violet-500/20 text-violet-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Release</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">AngelList USVC: $500 Minimum VC Fund</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">Apr 22, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">SF-based Rails platform opens a regulated venture fund to every U.S. investor at a $500 minimum. Naval Ravikant chairs. Holdings include OpenAI, Anthropic, xAI, Sierra, Crusoe, Vercel, Legora.</p>
                            <a href="https://www.crowdfundinsider.com/2026/04/274959-angellist-launches-usvc-a-regulated-venture-fund-available-to-everyone-minimum-investment-of-500/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Earnings: Omada -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Earnings</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Omada Crosses 1M Members, Joins Optum Rx GLP-1</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">May 7, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">SF Rails company posts Q1 revenue $78M (+42%), 1.02M members (+51%, first time over 1M), and adjusted EBITDA turned positive ($1M vs. -$4M a year ago). Joins Optum Rx's Weight Engage for GLP-1 access — now contracted with all three major PBMs — plus Eli Lilly Employer Connect. Raises 2026 guidance to $322–330M.</p>
                            <a href="https://www.globenewswire.com/news-release/2026/05/07/3290526/0/en/Omada-Health-Reports-First-Quarter-2026-Results.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                        <!-- Release: Doximity Clinical AI Suite -->
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8">
                            <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-violet-500/20 text-violet-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded mb-3">Release</span>
                            <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white mb-2">Doximity Ships Free Clinical AI Suite</h3>
                            <p class="text-xs text-white/40 mb-2">May 5, 2026</p>
                            <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed mb-3">SF-based Rails Foundation Core member bundles Ask, Scribe, and Dialer into one free product for U.S. clinicians. Scribe is already generating millions of clinical notes for 10K+ Doximity members in beta.</p>
                            <a href="https://blog.doximity.com/articles/introducing-the-doximity-clinical-ai-suite" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-violet-400 hover:text-violet-300 transition-colors">
                                Read more
                                <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                            </a>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Three Column Stories: Row 2 -->
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-8 md:gap-0 mb-6">
                        <div class="md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-emerald-500/20 text-emerald-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Acquisition</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Shopify Acquires Vantage Discovery</h3>
                                <p class="text-sm text-white/60 leading-relaxed">Rails Foundation Core member absorbs San Jose AI-search startup. Vantage's semantic search team joins Shopify's merchant + buyer AI stack. Adds to a Q1 of $3.2B revenue (+34%) and the first $100B+ GMV quarter.</p>
                                <a href="https://betakit.com/shopify-acquires-search-startup-vantage-discovery-for-undisclosed-amount/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-xs text-emerald-400 hover:text-emerald-300 transition-colors">
                                    Read more
                                    <svg class="w-3 h-3" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M17 8l4 4m0 0l-4 4m4-4H3" /></svg>
                                </a>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <div class="md:border-l md:border-white/10 md:pl-8 md:pr-8">
                            <div class="flex flex-col gap-3">
                                <span class="inline-block px-2.5 py-1 bg-violet-500/20 text-violet-400 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider rounded w-fit">Release</span>
                                <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-bold text-white">Gusto Spring Showcase Deepens Claude</h3>
